    <bpmn:process id="W_W3978" name="W3978. Inorganic Growth Strategy &amp; Build-vs-Buy-vs-Partner Framework" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Growth opportunity; capability gap; market-entry decision
Frequency: Per opportunity + maintained framework
Volume: Per strategic question
Owner: Head of Corporate Development / Strategy
Participants: Corp Dev, Strategy (links to VS-33.3), Insights (links to VS-44), Finance (links to VS-17.4), affected business unit, Legal (links to VS-100), Govt Affairs (links to VS-104)
Source: workflow W3978 — Inorganic Growth Strategy &amp; Build-vs-Buy-vs-Partner Framework</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3978_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3978_Lane1" name="Corp Dev">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3978_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3978_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3978_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3978_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3978_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3978_Start3" name="Growth opportunity; capability gap; market-entry decision">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3978_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3978_Task4" name="Corp Dev/Strategy apply the build-vs-buy-vs-partner framework to each growth…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Corp Dev/Strategy apply the build-vs-buy-vs-partner framework to each growth opportunity: organic build (store opening VS-37, capability build VS-123), acquisition (VS-130), JV/strategic alliance (links to W3963), licensing/franchise, or marketplace/3P extension (VS-95) — scoring on time-to-market, capability fit, cost, risk, and control
Responsible (R): Corp Dev / Strategy
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per opportunity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3978_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3978_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3978_Task5" name="Corp Dev assess market-entry mode for new geographies/categories (greenfield vs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Corp Dev assess market-entry mode for new geographies/categories (greenfield vs acquisition vs JV), regulatory/foreign-ownership considerations (links to VS-104/VS-87), and competitive/antitrust implications (links to VS-129 W3963/W3967)
Responsible (R): Corp Dev / Legal / Strategy
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per opportunity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3978_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3978_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3978_Task6" name="Corp Dev document the recommendation, seek approval (links to W3983), and route…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Corp Dev document the recommendation, seek approval (links to W3983), and route to the appropriate execution path
Responsible (R): Corp Dev
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per opportunity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3978_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3978_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3978_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3978_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3978_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-620 (ensure controlled execution — Corporate Development Strategy, Pipeline &amp; Target Identification (PA-130.1).) | - operational: structured framework; operational: regulatory and competitive analysis
Owner: Head of Corporate Development / Strategy</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3978_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3978_Annotation8" targetRef="W3978_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
